# Handler matrix

See [handlers](/docs/applications/handlers/) and the
[runtime](/docs/reference/runtime/) contract. Exhaustive handler matrix, not a
beginner walkthrough.

One standalone app that lists every accepted handler construct. Each fragment
verb morphs its own result well in the acting tab only (`#frag-get` through
`#frag-delete`). Commands still return no representation: Datastar gets empty
SSE, `curl` gets 204. `@get:live("/events/matrix")` owns `#live-tick` and
`#event-log` so the stream never races a one-shot fragment.

Click a fragment: that well fills immediately, and the shared SQLite log
updates in every tab. Click a command: the command card stays empty on
purpose; only the log moves. GET fragment is `data-on:click=@get(...)`, not a
navigation link.

This catalog row is **docs-only**. Do not expose it as a public origin; use
local `curl` against `rocci run`. Source files are listed in the sidebar.

## Run locally

```sh
cargo run -q -p rocci-cli -- run examples/rocci/standalone/handler-matrix/HandlerMatrix.rocci
```

Open the printed URL in two windows. Click a fragment in one; the other keeps
its wells and both logs update. Click a command; only the logs update.

## Smoke

```sh
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/health
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/post-frag
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/actions/post-cmd
```
